  ex:v39 a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Variability Occurs at Different Levels"@en ; cd:body "Compare sites, independent samples within a site, preparations within a sample, and instrumental repeats within a preparation. A lower-level repeat does not measure every higher-level source. Independent, additive variance components require an appropriate model; nesting alone does not establish them."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v39-flow a cd:FlowDiagram ; skos:prefLabel "A nested analytical workflow"@en ; cd:body "Each parent may have several children. The four boxes show levels, not four independent observations."@en ; cd:hasDiagramNode ex:v39-n1, ex:v39-n2, ex:v39-n3, ex:v39-n4 ; cd:hasDiagramEdge ex:v39-e1, ex:v39-e2, ex:v39-e3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v39-n1 a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Sampling site"@en ; cd:body "Between-site variation"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v39-n2 a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Independent sample"@en ; cd:body "Between samples within a site"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v39-n3 a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Sample preparation"@en ; cd:body "Between preparations of a sample"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v39-n4 a cd:DiagramNode ; cd:position 4 ; skos:prefLabel "Instrument repeat"@en ; cd:body "Instrumental replicates within a preparation"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v39-e1 a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 1 ; cd:sourceNode ex:v39-n1 ; cd:targetNode ex:v39-n2 ; skos:prefLabel "collect"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v39-e2 a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 2 ; cd:sourceNode ex:v39-n2 ; cd:targetNode ex:v39-n3 ; skos:prefLabel "prepare"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v39-e3 a cd:DiagramEdge ; cd:position 3 ; cd:sourceNode ex:v39-n3 ; cd:targetNode ex:v39-n4 ; skos:prefLabel "measure"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:v40 a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Lake Sampling: Within-Site and Between-Site Variation"@en ; cd:body "Same fifteen values as in Variables. Within-site spread compares three values at one site; between-site variation compares sites, for example their means. Observed differences do not identify causes: three values per site cannot separate sampling, preparation and instrument variance without a suitable experimental design."@en ; dct:source ex:dataset-lake-analyte-a-replicates ; cd:authoredResource true .
