  ex:v41 a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "What Counts as an Independent Replicate?"@en ; cd:body "The number of measurements is not necessarily the number of independent experimental units. An independent unit supplies separate evidence for the target question under the design and assumptions. Pseudoreplication counts dependent or nested readings as if they were such units; the label ‘replicate’ does not establish independence."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v-pseudoreplication a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "pseudoreplication"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:v-pseudo-def ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v-pseudo-def a cd:Definition ; cd:body "Treating measurements that are not independent replicates for the inferential target as if they were independent sampling units."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v41-cards a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:v41-a, ex:v41-b, ex:v41-c ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v41-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Three injections, one vial"@en ; cd:body "Technical replicates: repeated readings of the same material. Capture injection/instrument variation, not preparation or field-sampling variation. Shared drift can still cause dependence."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v41-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Three independent preparations"@en ; cd:body "Separately prepare aliquots of one sample. Can capture preparation plus downstream measurement variation. They share the field sample and are not three independent field units."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v41-c a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Three independent field samples"@en ; cd:body "Separately collect, prepare and measure samples. Can capture sampling plus downstream variation. Independent evidence for a field target depends on spatial/temporal design and shared conditions."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:v42 a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Degrees of Freedom Beyond the Mean"@en ; cd:body "For a linear model with a full-column-rank design matrix, residual df = n − p. Here p counts independent estimated model coefficients. This is a model-rank statement, not a universal formula for every statistical procedure."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v42-formula a cd:MathExpression ; cd:latex "\\mathrm{df}_{\\mathrm{res}}=n-p" ; dct:hasPart ex:v42-legend ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v42-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:v42-a, ex:v42-b, ex:v42-c ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v42-a a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "n observations, p estimable parameters"@en ; cd:body "X is the linear-model design matrix. For ordinary least squares, full column rank gives p independently estimable coefficients and p residual constraints. In general, residual df = n − rank(X)."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v42-b a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 2 ; skos:prefLabel "Estimate one mean"@en ; cd:body "p = 1: one intercept/mean. Residual df = n − 1."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v42-c a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 3 ; skos:prefLabel "Fit a straight line"@en ; cd:body "p = 2: intercept and slope. With distinct x values and full rank, residual df = n − 2."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .

  ex:v43 a cd:Interpretation ; skos:prefLabel "Residual Standard Deviation in Calibration"@en ; cd:body "Illustrative UV/Vis calibration: five standards, two fitted coefficients, three residual df. OLS fit: intercept 0.044 a.u.; slope 0.982 a.u. per mg/L; SS residual = 0.01824 a.u.²; s_res ≈ 0.07797 a.u. It measures response scatter about the fitted line, not concentration uncertainty."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v43-formula a cd:MathExpression ; cd:latex "\\begin{gathered}y_i=\\beta_0+\\beta_1x_i+\\varepsilon_i\\\\s_{\\mathrm{res}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\sum_i(y_i-\\hat{y}_i)^2}{n-2}}\\end{gathered}" ; dct:hasPart ex:v43-legend ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v43-legend a cd:DefinitionList ; cd:hasDefinitionListEntry ex:v43-key ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v43-key a cd:DefinitionListEntry ; cd:position 1 ; skos:prefLabel "Model and residuals"@en ; cd:body "xᵢ: standard concentration; yᵢ: observed response; ŷᵢ: predicted response. β₀: intercept; β₁: slope; εᵢ: model error. n − 2: residual df. Interpreting s_res as an error SD assumes independent zero-mean errors of common variance and a suitable linear model."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v43-data a cd:Dataset ; skos:prefLabel "Observed signals"@en ; cd:unit "a.u." ; dct:description "Illustrative UV/Vis calibration standards; concentrations 0, 1, 2, 3, 4 mg/L."@en ; cd:hasObservation ex:v43-o1, ex:v43-o2, ex:v43-o3, ex:v43-o4, ex:v43-o5 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v43-o1 a cd:Observation ; cd:position 1 ; cd:xValue 0.0 ; cd:numericValue 0.05 ; cd:authoredResource true .
  ex:v43-o2 a cd:Observation ; cd:position 2 ; cd:xValue 1.0 ; cd:numericValue 1.02 ; cd:authoredResource true .
